From e1884102b6c21bd51388f15378c4b97cdd77fce4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bench <bench@local>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 18:07:23 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] null patch: 76-client-level-model

A bot's block predictions are written into its own World, as vanilla's ClientLevel does, and the patch 53 overlay is gone. BotWorld, the predicted field, set_predicted, clear_predictions_in_chunk and has_override_in are removed; BlockView stays as the read interface. BlockStatePredictionHandler now holds the sequence, the acked sequence and, per pending cell, the sequence, the server's last state and the player position. Its methods follow the four rules of CLIENT_LEVEL_MODEL: predict_block (rule 1: write the level; keep the old state only if the cell changed; a pending cell keeps its first old state), set_server_verified (rule 2: a pending cell takes the update in its entry and the level is not written), end_predictions_up_to (rule 3: write the kept state where the level differs, then the caller's snap test) and a chunk packet or forget leaves the handler alone (rule 4). The new accessor server_block_state reads the entry's state for a pending cell, else the level; the patch 54 judgement (settle_block_actions) reads it. Readers in physics, entity, client and azalea no longer take the handler.

Vanilla, Mojang names: ClientLevel#setBlock, #setServerVerifiedBlockState, #syncBlockState; BlockStatePredictionHandler#retainKnownServerState, #updateKnownServerState, #endPredictionsUpTo; ClientPacketListener#updateLevelChunk. Closes the chunk-re-sent corner (edge a): the ack writes the kept state over the packet's block.
